{"app_id": 3, "name": "Pipedrive", "category": "CRM and Sales", "one_line_description": "Pipedrive offers a stable REST API for customizing CRM systems and creating integrations.", "auth_methods": ["OAuth2", "API key", "Basic"], "self_serve_status": "self_serve_free", "gating_detail": "Developers can register an app in the Pipedrive Marketplace to get a client ID for OAuth2, and can request a free sandbox account for testing.", "api_surface_summary": "Pipedrive provides a comprehensive RESTful API with JSON output, covering a wide range of CRM functionalities like deals, leads, organizations, persons, activities, and more. It offers OpenAPI 3 specification files for both v1 and v2 APIs, indicating good documentation.", "has_existing_mcp": true, "mcp_detail": "There are at least two community-developed open-source MCP servers for Pipedrive: one by ckalima with 155 tools (v2-first, MIT license) and another by GarethWright with 100 tools (94 wrapping the REST API and 6 custom analytics tools). Both are STDIO transport and use API keys for authentication.", "buildability_verdict": "ready_today", "main_blocker": null, "evidence_urls": ["https://developers.pipedrive.com/docs/api/v1/Oauth", "https://developers.pipedrive.com/docs/api/v1", "https://devcommunity.pipedrive.com/t/open-source-pipedrive-mcp-server-155-tools-v2-first-mit/20392", "https://www.pipedrive.com/en/features/crm-api", "https://devcommunity.pipedrive.com/t/pipedrive-mcp-server/20195", "https://apis.apievangelist.com/store/pipedrive-oauth-api"], "confidence": 1.0, "notes": null, "_meta": {"status": "ok", "seconds": 13.3, "evidence_urls_gathered": ["https://developers.pipedrive.com/docs/api/v1/Oauth", "https://developers.pipedrive.com/docs/api/v1", "https://devcommunity.pipedrive.com/t/open-source-pipedrive-mcp-server-155-tools-v2-first-mit/20392", "https://www.pipedrive.com/en/features/crm-api", "https://devcommunity.pipedrive.com/t/pipedrive-mcp-server/20195", "https://apis.apievangelist.com/store/pipedrive-oauth-api"]}}
{"app_id": 4, "name": "Attio", "category": "CRM and Sales", "one_line_description": "Attio is a CRM and relationship management tool designed for teams to manage customer relationships and automate sales processes.", "auth_methods": ["OAuth2", "API key", "Basic", "Token"], "self_serve_status": "self_serve_free", "gating_detail": "Developers can sign up for a free plan without a credit card, which includes API and webhook access. API keys can be generated in developer settings, and OAuth 2.0 flows are supported for multi-workspace apps.", "api_surface_summary": "Attio offers a comprehensive and well-structured REST API with an OpenAPI spec, covering CRUD operations for CRM entities like records, lists, notes, tasks, files, meetings, and call recordings, along with webhooks.", "has_existing_mcp": true, "mcp_detail": "Attio provides an official MCP server, which is accessible even on the free plan.", "buildability_verdict": "ready_today", "main_blocker": null, "evidence_urls": ["https://docs.attio.com/rest-api/guides/authentication", "https://attio.com/pricing", "https://www.coffee.ai/articles/attio-crm-public-api-docs", "https://getknit.dev/blog/build-an-attio-api-integration-for-crm-data-sync", "https://apis.apievangelist.com/store/attio-files-api", "https://apis.io/apis/attio/attio-oauth-api"], "confidence": 0.9, "notes": null, "_meta": {"status": "ok", "seconds": 14.6, "evidence_urls_gathered": ["https://docs.attio.com/rest-api/guides/authentication", "https://attio.com/pricing", "https://www.coffee.ai/articles/attio-crm-public-api-docs", "https://getknit.dev/blog/build-an-attio-api-integration-for-crm-data-sync", "https://apis.apievangelist.com/store/attio-files-api", "https://apis.io/apis/attio/attio-oauth-api"]}}
{"app_id": 2, "name": "HubSpot", "category": "CRM and Sales", "one_line_description": "HubSpot provides APIs for developers to build apps that integrate with its CRM data and functionality, supporting various authentication methods.", "auth_methods": ["OAuth2", "API key", "Token"], "self_serve_status": "unknown", "gating_detail": "Developers can obtain API keys and static access tokens from their HubSpot account's developer overview or app settings after creating an app. The specific requirements (e.g., paid plan) for accessing the developer platform are not detailed in the provided evidence.", "api_surface_summary": "HubSpot offers a broad REST API surface, indicated by mentions of various endpoints and OpenAPI definitions, covering CRM data like contacts, deals, and engagements, with detailed documentation for authentication.", "has_existing_mcp": true, "mcp_detail": "HubSpot offers two distinct MCP servers: a remote HubSpot MCP server for connecting AI tools or agents to CRM data with read and write access, and a developer MCP server for local app development via the CLI. Both support OAuth 2.0.", "buildability_verdict": "ready_today", "main_blocker": null, "evidence_urls": ["https://developers.hubspot.com/docs/apps/developer-platform/build-apps/authentication/overview", "https://developers.hubspot.com/docs/apps/legacy-apps/authentication/intro-to-auth", "https://developers.hubspot.com/ai-tools/mcp", "https://developers.hubspot.com/docs/apps/developer-platform/build-apps/integrate-with-the-remote-hubspot-mcp-server", "https://www.postman.com/hubspot/hubspot-public-api-workspace/overview", "https://apis.io/security/hubspot/hubspot-authentication"], "confidence": 0.9, "notes": "The evidence clearly outlines multiple authentication methods and the existence of dedicated MCP servers for AI agents. The primary unknown is whether a paid HubSpot plan is required to access the developer platform and obtain API credentials, as this is not explicitly stated.", "_meta": {"status": "ok", "seconds": 16.8, "evidence_urls_gathered": ["https://developers.hubspot.com/docs/apps/developer-platform/build-apps/authentication/overview", "https://developers.hubspot.com/docs/apps/legacy-apps/authentication/intro-to-auth", "https://developers.hubspot.com/ai-tools/mcp", "https://developers.hubspot.com/docs/apps/developer-platform/build-apps/integrate-with-the-remote-hubspot-mcp-server", "https://www.postman.com/hubspot/hubspot-public-api-workspace/overview", "https://apis.io/security/hubspot/hubspot-authentication"]}}
{"app_id": 1, "name": "Salesforce", "category": "CRM and Sales", "one_line_description": "Salesforce offers hosted Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers that expose an organization's logic and assets, including data, flows, Apex actions, and queries, to AI clients.", "auth_methods": ["OAuth2", "Token", "Basic"], "self_serve_status": "gated_paid_plan", "gating_detail": "Access to hosted MCP servers and API credentials requires an existing Salesforce Enterprise Edition org or above, and System Administrator permissions to configure an External Client App.", "api_surface_summary": "The API surface is broad, exposing org logic, data, flows, Apex actions, and queries via MCP, alongside existing REST APIs, Named Query APIs, and SOQL queries. The documentation includes developer blogs and setup guides, indicating it is well-documented.", "has_existing_mcp": true, "mcp_detail": "Salesforce hosted MCP servers are generally available, providing a Salesforce-managed endpoint that exposes org logic and assets to any MCP-compatible AI client, with built-in enterprise-grade authentication and governance.", "buildability_verdict": "ready_today", "main_blocker": null, "evidence_urls": ["https://developer.salesforce.com/blogs/2026/04/salesforce-hosted-mcp-servers-are-now-generally-available", "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/hosted-mcp-servers/guide/setup-overview.html", "https://documentation.sailpoint.com/connectors/salesforce/va/help/configuring_legacy_authentication.html", "https://ta.thinkingdata.cn/trino-docs/security/salesforce.html", "https://trino.io/docs/current/security/salesforce.html", "https://docs-snow.flexera.com/snow-atlas/user-documentation/saas/saas-connectors/prepare-salesforce-sales-cloud-connector/api-calls-for-salesforce-sales-cloud"], "confidence": 0.9, "notes": "The primary authentication method for MCP is OAuth 2.0 with PKCE. Other evidence snippets also indicate support for password-based authentication with a security token (which can be categorized as Token or Basic), though a password grant type is noted as deprecated.", "_meta": {"status": "ok", "seconds": 17.4, "evidence_urls_gathered": ["https://developer.salesforce.com/blogs/2026/04/salesforce-hosted-mcp-servers-are-now-generally-available", "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/hosted-mcp-servers/guide/setup-overview.html", "https://documentation.sailpoint.com/connectors/salesforce/va/help/configuring_legacy_authentication.html", "https://ta.thinkingdata.cn/trino-docs/security/salesforce.html", "https://trino.io/docs/current/security/salesforce.html", "https://docs-snow.flexera.com/snow-atlas/user-documentation/saas/saas-connectors/prepare-salesforce-sales-cloud-connector/api-calls-for-salesforce-sales-cloud"]}}
{"app_id": 5, "name": "Twenty", "category": "CRM and Sales", "one_line_description": "Twenty is an open-source CRM that provides REST and GraphQL APIs for managing CRM data and schema.", "auth_methods": ["API key", "OAuth2"], "self_serve_status": "self_serve_free", "gating_detail": "Developers can create an API key directly from their workspace settings or dynamically register an OAuth client, and the API is available on the free plan.", "api_surface_summary": "Twenty offers both REST and GraphQL APIs, generated from the workspace schema, covering Core API for CRUD operations on records (People, Companies, Opportunities, custom objects) and Metadata API for schema management. Workspace-specific API documentation with an interactive playground is available after creating an API key.", "has_existing_mcp": true, "mcp_detail": "Every Cloud workspace ships with a native MCP server, allowing AI assistants to connect via OAuth to read and write CRM data in natural language.", "buildability_verdict": "ready_today", "main_blocker": null, "evidence_urls": ["https://docs.twenty.com/developers/extend/api", "https://docs.twenty.com/developers/extend/oauth", "https://twenty.com/pricing", "https://mindcloud.co/docs/universal/rest/twenty/0.0.5/introduction/authentication", "https://apis.apievangelist.com/store/twenty-open-api-api", "https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/issues/10283"], "confidence": 1.0, "notes": null, "_meta": {"status": "ok", "seconds": 10.6, "evidence_urls_gathered": ["https://docs.twenty.com/developers/extend/api", "https://docs.twenty.com/developers/extend/oauth", "https://twenty.com/pricing", "https://mindcloud.co/docs/universal/rest/twenty/0.0.5/introduction/authentication", "https://apis.apievangelist.com/store/twenty-open-api-api", "https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/issues/10283"]}}
